  "description": "T1. Bull bay Magnolia Tree. 12 metres in height. 10 metres in width. Reduce height by 2 metres, leaving the tree 10 metres in height and laterally reduce by up to 1 metre to reshape, this would leave the tree 9 metres in width. Roots of the Magnolia is obstructing the pathway/ slabs next door so reducing the tree will stop the roots from spreading. Remove 2 small limbs that are sitting on the fence. Overgrown and growing over fence. Situated in the rear garden.\rT2. Tulip Tree. 13.8 metres in height. Reduce branches to 50cms away from street sign, back to closest growth point and crown lift to 3 metres above ground level, over pavement. Tree overhangs the pavement and the TFL signs. Situated in the front garden.\rT3. Bird Cherry Tree. 4.6 metres in height. Crown lift to 2.4 metres above ground level over pavement. The canopy is overhanging the pavement. Situated in the rear garden.",
